+//! A small evaluator for a subset of the Forth programming language.
+//!
+//! The evaluator supports integer arithmetic (`+`, `-`, `*`, `/`), the stack
+//! manipulation words `DUP`, `DROP`, `SWAP` and `OVER`, and user defined words
+//! declared with `: name definition ;`.
+//!
+//! Words are resolved against the definitions that exist *at the moment they
+//! are parsed*. A user defined word therefore keeps referring to whatever the
+//! referenced words meant when it was defined, which is what makes the
+//! redefinition semantics of Forth work. Bodies are stored once and shared
+//! through `Rc`, so defining a word in terms of other words never expands them
+//! (and therefore cannot be used as an allocation attack).
